# Line endings are LF in this repo and must stay LF.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Both this repo and the canonical my-powerhouse store LF in
# git. The trap is a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true: it checks files out
# as CRLF and converts them back on commit. If that conversion ever lands, every
# line of every file shows as changed. A review of that diff is worthless, and
# so is the rollback diff you would need if the deploy came up wrong.
#
# Measured 2026-08-20, before the first sync in four months: all blobs LF on
# both sides, and the sync diff was identical with and without
# --ignore-cr-at-eol (732 changed lines either way). That is the proof no
# line-ending noise reached the commit. This file is what keeps it true for
# whoever syncs next, from whatever machine.
#
# Committed on its own, ahead of the code, so the guard is in force when the
# code lands and a revert of the code does not take the guard with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.jpg -text
*.png -text
*.pdf -text
